/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 1:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the structural taxonomy of the eight traditional parts of speech and discuss their specific syntactic functions in technical scientific prose.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Foundations & Grammatical Taxonomy:) Tj
T*
(   In English morphology and syntax, words are classified into eight core parts of speech based on) Tj
T*
(   their syntactic role, inflectional properties, and semantic value:) Tj
T*
(   - Nouns \(Substantives\): Act as clause heads \(subjects, direct objects, indirect objects,) Tj
T*
(   objects of prepositions\). In technical registers, nouns carry dense scientific information) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., oligonucleotide, bioreactor, luminescence\).) Tj
T*
(   - Pronouns: Anaphoric substitutes that maintain syntactic economy and cohesion while avoiding) Tj
T*
(   tedious nominal repetition.) Tj
T*
(   - Verbs: The relational core of clauses conveying states, processes, enzymatic transformations,) Tj
T*
(   and physical phenomena.) Tj
T*
(   - Adjectives: Modifiers restricting or qualifying nominal referents \(e.g., thermophilic,) Tj
T*
(   non-polar, double-blind\).) Tj
T*
(   - Adverbs: Modifiers specifying manner, degree, temporal frequency, or clause transitions.) Tj
T*
(   - Prepositions: Closed-class relational heads establishing spatio-temporal and conceptual links) Tj
T*
(   between noun phrases and other clause elements.) Tj
T*
(   - Conjunctions: Syntactic linkers \(coordinating, subordinating, correlative\) governing logical) Tj
T*
(   clause dependencies.) Tj
T*
(   - Interjections: Expressive tokens strictly excluded from formal scientific and academic) Tj
T*
(   manuscripts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Syntactic Function in Scientific Registers:) Tj
T*
(   Scientific communication demands high lexical density, precision, and objectivity. This) Tj
T*
(   requires balancing nominalizations with active verbal predicates to maintain clarity without) Tj
T*
(   obscuring causal agentivity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Morphological and Syntactic Diagnostics:) Tj
T*
(   - Form-Class Words: Nouns, verbs, adjectives, and adverbs accept derivational affixes and) Tj
T*
(   represent an open vocabulary.) Tj
T*
(   - Structure-Class Words: Prepositions, pronouns, conjunctions, and determiners form closed) Tj
T*
(   systems establishing grammatical scaffolding.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 2:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine the grammatical distinction between countable and uncountable \(mass\) nouns in biotechnology, detailing common mass noun errors.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Countable vs. Mass Noun Mechanics:) Tj
T*
(   - Countable Nouns: Refer to discrete, quantifiable physical entities that possess regular) Tj
T*
(   plural inflections \(-s, -es\) and accept indefinite articles \(a, an\) or cardinal numerals \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   one plasmid, two colonies, five micropipettes\).) Tj
T*
(   - Uncountable \(Mass\) Nouns: Refer to undifferentiated aggregates, substances, liquids, abstract) Tj
T*
(   properties, or collective apparatuses. They cannot take indefinite articles \(*an equipment\) and) Tj
T*
(   lack plural inflections \(*equipments\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Common Mass Noun Pitfalls in Biotechnology Literature:) Tj
T*
(   - Apparatus: Functions as a mass noun or takes zero-plural / apparatuses depending on register.) Tj
T*
(   Strictly avoid *apparata.) Tj
T*
(   - Equipment: Strictly uncountable. Correct usage: "several pieces of equipment" or "specialized) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
