(>> Solution to Question 3:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the role of nominalization in academic scientific discourse, evaluating both its stylistic benefits and cognitive disadvantages.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Nature of Nominalization:) Tj
T*
(   Nominalization is the morphological derivation of abstract nouns from verbs or adjectives) Tj
T*
(   \(e.g., analyze -> analysis; precipitate -> precipitation; permeable -> permeability; bind ->) Tj
T*
(   binding\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Stylistic Benefits in Research Writing:) Tj
T*
(   - Condensation and Lexical Density: Encapsulates complex mechanical procedures into single) Tj
T*
(   thematic subject nouns, facilitating technical synthesis.) Tj
T*
(   - Objective Depersonalization: Shifting focus from human researchers \("We isolated the) Tj
T*
(   protein"\) to the biochemical event itself \("Isolation of the protein was performed"\).) Tj
T*
(   - Syntactic Thematization \(Given-New Information Flow\): Allows the result of a previous) Tj
T*
(   sentence to become the thematic topic of the subsequent clause \(e.g., "...producing a brown) Tj
T*
(   precipitate. This precipitation indicated..."\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Cognitive Drawbacks and Grammatical Smothering:) Tj
T*
(   - Buried Verbs \(Zombie Nouns\): Over-nominalization suffocates vigorous action under heavy noun) Tj
T*
(   stacks, forcing reliance on weak linking verbs like "take place", "occur", or "be".) Tj
T*
(   - Example: "A calculation of the yield was conducted by the team" vs. Active: "The team) Tj
T*
(   calculated the yield.") Tj
T*
(   - Readability Optimization: Strive for equilibrium; deploy nominalizations for thematic) Tj
T*
(   cohesion, but preserve finite active verbs for core experimental procedures.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 4:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the rules governing subject-verb agreement \(concord\) with collective nouns in American versus British scientific English.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Theoretical Framework of Concord:) Tj
T*
(   Collective nouns \(e.g., team, panel, committee, cohort, species, family, group\) designate an) Tj
T*
(   assemblage of individual members treated as an integrated entity.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Dialectical Conventions:) Tj
T*
(   - American English \(Formal Academic Standard\): Treats collective nouns as singular units) Tj
T*
(   representing an undivided corporate body, mandating singular verbs and singular pronouns:) Tj
T*
