(>> Solution to Question 7:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss indefinite pronouns and their subject-verb concord rules, focusing on tricky indefinite quantifiers in laboratory contexts.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Singular Indefinite Pronouns:) Tj
T*
(   The following indefinite pronouns are grammatically singular and mandate singular verbs,) Tj
T*
(   regardless of intervening plural prepositional phrases:) Tj
T*
(   - Each, either, neither, one, everyone, everybody, anyone, anybody, no one, nobody, someone,) Tj
T*
(   somebody.) Tj
T*
(   - Example: "Each of the ninety-six wells contains a micro-liter of substrate." \(Contains, not) Tj
T*
(   contain\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Variable Indefinite Pronouns \(The SANAM Rule\):) Tj
T*
(   The pronouns Some, Any, None, All, More/Most change concord based on the object of the) Tj
T*
(   following preposition:) Tj
T*
(   - If the object is a mass noun: Singular verb \("Some of the buffer was spilled"; "None of the) Tj
T*
(   DNA was degraded"\).) Tj
T*
(   - If the object is a countable plural noun: Plural verb \("Some of the colonies were resistant";) Tj
T*
(   "None of the tubes were labeled"\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. 'None' in Academic Style:) Tj
T*
(   While historically parsed as 'not one' \(singular\), modern scientific usage treats 'none') Tj
T*
(   according to notional concord: "None of the samples were contaminated.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 8:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Distinguish finite from non-finite verbs, classifying gerunds, participles, and infinitives in technical protocols.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Finite Verbs:) Tj
T*
(   Carry grammatical tense \(past, present, future\), person \(first, second, third\), and number) Tj
T*
(   \(singular, plural\). They form the essential predicate head of independent and dependent) Tj
T*
(   clauses:) Tj
T*
(   - Example: "The autoclave sterilizes nutrient agar at 121 deg C for 15 minutes.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Non-Finite Verbs:) Tj
T*
(   Do not indicate tense or subject agreement independently. They comprise three structural) Tj
T*
(   classes:) Tj
T*
(   - Gerunds: Verb forms ending in -ing that function nominally as subjects, objects, or) Tj
T*
(   prepositional complements:) Tj
T*
(   - "Centrifuging at high speed pelleted the cellular debris." \(Subject\).) Tj
T*
(   - Participles: Verbal adjectives functioning as modifiers or components of aspectual) Tj
T*
(   periphrases:) Tj
T*
(   - Present Participle \(-ing\): "The expanding culture exhausted dissolved oxygen.") Tj
T*
(   - Past Participle \(-ed/-en\): "The denatured enzyme lost catalytic activity.") Tj
T*
(   - Infinitives: Base verb preceded by 'to' \(or bare infinitive\), functioning nominally,) Tj
T*
ET

