/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss the taxonomy of adverbs and analyze the placement of limiting adverbs like 'only', 'merely', and 'almost'.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Adverb Functional Classification:) Tj
T*
(   - Adverbs of Manner: Describe the mechanism or quality of action \(rapidly, uniformly,) Tj
T*
(   vigorously\).) Tj
T*
(   - Adverbs of Degree: Quantify intensity \(extremely, partially, substantially, moderately\).) Tj
T*
(   - Adverbs of Frequency: Denote recurrence \(frequently, occasionally, rarely\).) Tj
T*
(   - Adverbs of Time: Anchor chronology \(previously, subsequently, concurrently\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Limiting Adverbs and Syntactic Misplacement:) Tj
T*
(   Limiting adverbs \(only, merely, almost, nearly, just\) must be placed immediately adjacent to) Tj
T*
(   the specific syntactic constituent they modify:) Tj
T*
(   - Ambiguity 1: "The assay only detected three viral genomes." \(Implies the assay did nothing) Tj
T*
(   else except detect\).) Tj
T*
(   - Ambiguity 2: "Only the assay detected three viral genomes." \(Implies no other instrument) Tj
T*
(   detected them\).) Tj
T*
(   - Correct Academic Precision: "The assay detected only three viral genomes." \(Modifies the) Tj
T*
(   numeral 'three', emphasizing quantity\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
