12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Examine conjunctive adverbs in technical scientific transitions, punctuation requirements, and semicolon usage.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Definition and Functional Role:) Tj
T*
(   Conjunctive adverbs \(also called transition words\) connect two independent clauses by) Tj
T*
(   illustrating logical relationships such as causality, contrast, concession, or sequence:) Tj
T*
(   - Examples: however, therefore, furthermore, consequently, nevertheless, moreover,) Tj
T*
(   specifically.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Punctuation Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - Semicolon-Comma Construction: When joining two independent clauses in a compound sentence, a) Tj
T*
(   conjunctive adverb must be preceded by a semicolon and followed by a comma:) Tj
T*
(   - Correct: "The wild-type strain survived antibiotic exposure; however, the knockout mutant was) Tj
T*
ET

