ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Detail the rules governing gender-neutral pronoun usage and avoidance of bias in contemporary biomedical writing.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Historical Precedent vs. Modern Academic Standards:) Tj
T*
(   Historical scientific writing frequently used the generic masculine pronoun \('he', 'his'\) to) Tj
T*
(   refer to unspecified individuals, which modern academic bodies \(APA, IEEE, Nature, NIH\) reject) Tj
T*
(   as exclusionary.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Modern Strategies for Gender-Neutral Syntax:) Tj
T*
(   - Strategy 1: Pluralization \(Most natural in research\):) Tj
T*
(   - Biased: "Each participant recorded his symptoms.") Tj
T*
(   - Revised: "All participants recorded their symptoms.") Tj
T*
(   - Strategy 2: Paired Pronouns:) Tj
T*
(   - "Each participant recorded his or her symptoms.") Tj
T*
(   - Strategy 3: Singular 'They':) Tj
T*
(   - The singular 'they' \(and its inflections them, their, theirs\) is now fully endorsed by the) Tj
T*
(   Oxford English Dictionary, APA 7th Edition, and Chicago Manual of Style when referring to an) Tj
T*
(   individual whose gender is unspecified or non-binary:) Tj
T*
(   - "The patient was informed that they could withdraw from the trial at any time.") Tj
T*
(   - Strategy 4: Passive Rephrasing or Nominal Substitution:) Tj
T*
(   - "Each participant recorded symptoms in a personal clinical log.") Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 25:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze prepositions of time: 'at', 'on', 'in', 'during', and 'for' in laboratory protocol documentation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Prepositional Time Rules:) Tj
T*
(   - At: Used for precise, discrete clock times, specific temperatures, or distinct operational) Tj
T*
(   points:) Tj
T*
(   - "The assay commenced at 08:30 AM.") Tj
T*
(   - "Cell lysis occurs at 4 deg C.") Tj
T*
(   - On: Used for specific calendar days and dates:) Tj
T*
(   - "Samples were harvested on Monday, October 12.") Tj
T*
(   - In: Used for non-specific broad intervals \(months, years, decades\) or elapsed durations until) Tj
T*
(   an event:) Tj
T*
(   - "The recombinant strain was developed in 2024.") Tj
T*
(   - "The pellet will dissolve in five minutes.") Tj
T*
ET

